3	// Server actions for the native webmail "Mailbox settings" panel
4	// (components/customer/mail/MailSettings.tsx, opened from the FolderRail).
5	//
6	// Every action authenticates the caller and resolves ONLY a mailbox they own via
7	// `resolveMailbox` (which also performs the ownership check used everywhere else
8	// in the mail client). Writes are rate-limited and return a friendly
9	// `{ ok, error }`. Anything that changes mail ROUTING — aliases, forwarding,
10	// auto-reply — additionally requires the target domain to be on a VERIFIED
11	// subscription owned by the caller before touching Mailcow.
12	//
13	// Identity + signature live on the Mailbox row (and are read by
14	// lib/actions-mail.ts when sending). Auto-reply and forwarding are compiled to
15	// sieve and pushed to Mailcow — see lib/mail/sieve.ts.
16	//
17	// Storage quota is displayed only; the plan tier sets it, so there is no
18	// customer-facing write for it here.
19	
